# Git Workflow

Before creating any branch, commit, push, or PR, follow the **`git-commit` skill**. It is the source of
truth for branch naming, safe branching, commit-message format (commitlint), the OpenSpec
`feature/<name>` flow with an **opt-in** `requirements/<name>` branch (offered only when a change has an
FSD/ISD, for a clean review diff; single-branch otherwise), and the push/PR gate.

**Never** push to a protected branch (`develop` / `main` / `master`). Branch off the integration branch
with `--no-track`.
